      "artist": "Michael Gunther",
      "description": "Candi Kalasan is located in the area of Prambanan, a few km NE of Yogyakarta. The temple is dated by inscription to 778 AD, and is dedicated to Tara. It has been only partially restored, but is notable for some fine remaining carvings.\nThe current view of the temple grounds is quite misleading;  originally the temple was surrounded by 52 stupas, that contained caskets and other funerary remains on the grounds of this large royal cemetery.\nThe north face of the temple is seen here.",
